# R1 first-pass preservation and descriptive summary

This plan adds evaluator custody instruments only. `preserve_first_pass.py`,
`summarize.py`, this plan, the independent custody review and the unchanged
`../acquisition_summary.py` must appear in the implementation freeze's
`verification_files`. Their identical entries remain in the campaign freeze.
No collector, scorer, learner, fixture, oracle or retained measurement helper is
changed. Authoring and review use public code and metadata, without reading R1
raw evidence or the sealed specification, report or application semantics.

## Fixed first pass

The raw root is `../first_pass/reservoir`. Initial collection is
`r1_initial_v1`; candidate preparation writes
`r1_candidates_v1/candidates.json`. The four acquisition directories, in order,
are `r1_contested_1701`, `r1_untargeted_1701`, `r1_contested_1702` and
`r1_untargeted_1702`. Common evaluation is `r1_evaluation_v1`. Each of the five
training stages has `scores/<actual-stage>.json` under this directory.

The fixed jobs under `jobs/` are `r1_fixture_service_v1`, the initial stage,
`r1_candidates_v1`, the four arms, the evaluation stage and
`score_<actual-training-stage>` for all five trainings. All use the existing
`../run_job.py` record schema. The exact service command is
`.venv/bin/python experiments/transport_v1/server.py --port 8767`.
Collection commands follow the public envelope, with every option explicit;
acquisition includes `--initial`, `--policy`, `--budget 60` and its seed.
Preparation uses `--train`, `--out-dir` and the implementation freeze. Scoring
uses `--train`, `--eval`, `--candidates`, `--out` and the campaign freeze.
The instrument accepts relative or absolute repository file arguments and
arbitrary option order, but rejects missing, repeated or additional options.
The job root must be an actual directory containing exactly the 13 declared
job directories. Additional jobs, top-level files, symlinks and special entries
are rejected. This membership snapshot is rechecked before manifest writing.

The user's 20:01 UTC resource instruction restores the prior 12-core allowance
before any R1 execution. Root launches new workers under `taskset` within CPUs
12–23 at normal priority, with one numerical thread and `PYTHONHASHSEED=0`.
The process record authenticates
the thread environment; the outer CPU/priority launch and runner reaping remain
root's process-ownership responsibility because the retained runner does not
record its outer affinity or priority. The service lifetime covers all browser
collection. Root interrupts and reaps it after evaluation, before scoring;
its required terminal record is `INTERRUPTED`, return code `-15`,
`child_terminated: true`. Every other fixed job must be `FINISHED`, return code
zero and child-terminated. The five independent scores may run concurrently
after the service is reaped, within available memory. Initial collection,
candidate preparation, the declared arms
and evaluation must occur sequentially in their declared order.

## Preservation checks

The preserver uses the standard library and reads no sealed JSON semantics. It
authenticates both freeze phases, actual HEAD, the exact parent association and
all runtime, sealed and verification inventories. The campaign must add exactly
the initial observations, initial steps and candidate file to its parent's
runtime inventory. Sealed inventory entries must agree with the freeze. Both
opaque scripted inputs and the service source must be sealed commitments.

Each raw directory is inventoried completely. Charged decisions must be
consecutive; the single unpaired reset and observed reload must be retained;
paired decisions must match their raw steps field-for-field, and observations
must cover every referenced signature. Public predicted denominators are
checked against the records: initial 37 attempts/36 paired steps, evaluation
51/50 with ten distinct designated click targets, and each arm 60/59.
Each arm must preserve the exact initial raw byte prefixes and the refit
opportunities at charged counts 0, 15, 30 and 45. Recognized learned input
sidecars must be absent. All collected ledgers are bound to their owned child,
recorded arguments, timestamps, source and proper phase freeze.

The preserver executes unchanged `require`/`accounting` function AST nodes from
the authenticated retained summary, using only their original `Counter` and
budget globals. It executes the unchanged scorer `outcome_summary` function
with authenticated literal constants from `outcome.py`. This reuses the
retained accounting semantics without importing learner or native modules.
No AST body, condition or returned measurement is rewritten.

Candidate source, initial input version, freeze and candidate digest/count/
omission order must agree. Every score must retain the exact frozen candidate
IDs plus `current_inferred`, bind the correct candidate reading, and use the
same source, phase freeze and common evaluation version. All optional input
sidecar names and byte lengths are included in version checks. Every click
must remain in all three emission channels, query records and state opportunity
ledgers, including failed and unreachable attempts. Emission summaries are
recomputed with the unchanged retained function; category totals must cover
every click. No accuracy, binding quality, successful fit, target action
success, recognition success or hypothesis acceptance is a preservation gate.
Script `complete: false` is retained because the collector uses that field for
action success; full ledgers and completed jobs establish collection completion.

All fixed job source inventories, exact child commands and log hashes are
checked. All SemABI Python sources, frozen instruments, raw outputs, candidates,
scores, fixed job outputs and opaque sealed/control/adapter/helper bytes enter
the manifest. File hashes and output directory membership are checked again
before writing. The fixed output `first_pass_manifest_v1.json` is created
exclusively, never overwritten, with `status: PRESERVED` and a repository-relative
`files` map whose values are SHA-256 strings. This is the generic binding
adapter's required format. Stdout contains only output path, hash, status and
file count. Preservation does not infer scientific success.

## Summary adapter

Only after preservation, `summarize.py` calls the unchanged retained helper's
`summarize_fixture(inputs, "reservoir")`. Its exact read-only aliases map
`initial_v2` to `r1_initial_v1`, `evaluation_v2` to `r1_evaluation_v1`,
`candidates_v2/candidates.json` to `r1_candidates_v1/candidates.json`, and each
legacy arm name to the corresponding `r1_` arm. Logical score names map to
this directory's actual `scores/<r1-stage>.json` paths. Every other logical
input is rejected. No T1 fallback exists.

The adapter authenticates each consumed byte against the preservation manifest
before JSON parsing, and authenticates the repository code dependency inventory
before importing the retained helper. Initial and acquired raw input bytes are
also rechecked. It validates the actual R1 source/freeze associations and
rechecks all authenticated bytes before writing. Imports disable bytecode
writes; no fit, browser action, application module or evaluator control is
invoked. Normal Python dependency imports are the same as the retained helper.

Returned stage and support-reference names retain the helper's legacy logical
labels. The result explicitly includes stage aliases, every logical-to-actual
path, actual R1 source and freeze associations, the preservation digest,
dependency hashes and consumed input hashes. Fixed task targets, support,
observed vocabulary, identity comparisons and paired-seed comparisons all use
the original helper functions without semantic changes. A saved vouch remains
a representative support example, not an enumeration of supporting conjunctions.
The default exclusive output is `acquisition_summary_v1.json`; `--out` can name
another new JSON file directly in this directory. Only metadata is printed.

## Review and execution boundary

Author checks are limited to small standard-library AST/syntax and synthetic
adapter/custody checks within the current resource allowance. They must not read
actual R1 records, run native fits, launch browsers or execute controls.
Root independently reviews and commits these instruments before producing the
implementation freeze. Any rejected draft must be retained before revision.
Real preservation waits for the complete fixed pass. Summary and sealed
diagnostic controls wait for the resulting first-pass manifest. Later diagnosis
or repair cannot overwrite that manifest or any first-pass input.
Root invokes preservation directly on one CPU within the current allowance after
all 13 owned jobs are reaped; preservation must not create another job directory
under the fixed `jobs/` root. The rejected pre-review instrument and plan are
retained byte-for-byte under `instrument_revisions/` with the
`before_job_inventory` suffix. The independent job-inventory reproducer and its
before/after results remain under `review_evidence/`.

The accepted pre-resource-change protocol, plan, preserver and freezer remain
under `instrument_revisions` with `before_resource_restore` in their names.
`resource_review_v1.md` separately reviews the scheduling and dependency changes;
it and the resource override enter both phase freezes. The historical custody
review remains unchanged. Removing the score-overlap restriction does not relax
job membership, provenance, raw accounting, failure preservation or completion.
